    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0751" n="645" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg645"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial German Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic">February 26,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Permit me, in connection
                    with my statements of this morning, to inclose a memorandum explaining the
                    status of our new customs law. Could I ask you to be so kind as to send me a
                    short notice of the date on which the proclamation of the President regarding
                    section 3 of the Dingley tariff will be issued?</p>
                <p>Believe me, Mr. Secretary, most sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sternburg.</hi></signed></closer>




